+# TanStack Charts adapter-first migration — decisions
+
+## Locked PLAN decisions
+
+1. `@product-suite/ui-charting` is the permanent product boundary; apps never import a chart engine or its types/selectors.
+2. The modern candidate is `@tanstack/charts`, not the stale `react-charts` beta package.
+3. As of 2026-08-10, registry latest is exactly `0.9.0` and TanStack labels it pre-alpha/not production-ready. DEV is blocked until a human chooses wait-for-beta or explicitly accepts a non-production pre-alpha pilot.
+4. Any approved version is exact-pinned. Version upgrades are reviewed adapter changes with the full contract suite.
+5. The adapter exposes finite product semantics (time series, categorical bars, donut, radial gauge, states and export), never TanStack grammar objects.
+6. SVG is the only initial renderer. Canvas and new chart families require separate measured evidence.
+7. Migration is eight sequential PRs: shared foundation -> Platform cleanup -> Meeting migration -> deletion-only Meeting wrapper retirement -> Roadmap analytics -> Roadmap strategy -> E2E/visual parity -> post-observation dependency/docs retirement.
+8. Every app migration PR is capped at 300 added/modified production lines and must rebase/test against the preceding merged PR. The 319-line dead Meeting wrapper has its own deletion-only PR with zero replacement production code.
+9. Recharts remains available until the last consumer and rollback window finish; final removal is a separate PR.
+10. Stable product selectors and semantic/accessibility assertions replace engine DOM selectors. Visual baselines supplement, not replace, semantic tests.
+11. Historical research/plans are preserved as history; current authority docs receive the superseding decision.
+12. This refactor remains behind the meeting-capture critical path.
+13. Every adapter chart requires product wording for an exact-value summary/caption; ui-charting derives and links the semantic table from the same normalized plotted data and keeps it available when the engine fails.
+14. Final dependency removal requires a human-reviewed 14-consecutive-day window with exact-SHA green CI, route traffic thresholds, zero attributable chart errors, <=0.1 percentage-point error-rate delta, stable deterministic visual baselines, and start/end keyboard plus screen-reader checks. Low traffic extends the window.
+
+## Human decision required before DEV
+
+**Question:** Accept `@tanstack/charts@0.9.0` despite TanStack's pre-alpha/not-production-ready warning, strictly as a non-production adapter pilot, or wait for an official beta? Approval also locks the eight-PR train and 14-day observation/rollback exit contract.
+
+**Recommended:** wait for official beta and refresh registry/API evidence. If speed of learning outweighs churn risk, approve only the isolated non-production pilot; app rollout remains blocked until parity, accessibility, export, visual and rollback evidence is green.
+
+## PLAN execution notes
+
+- Forge claim was proven with the live lease before issue mutation.
+- The exact requested base was used in an isolated worktree.
+- No package was installed and no product code was edited.
+- The Forge PLAN adapter remains blocked on its legacy standalone `docs/research/tanstack-charts-adapter.md` prerequisite. This plan embeds the verified official research instead; the blocker is recorded rather than bypassed or repeatedly bootstrapped.
