+# TanStack Charts adapter-first migration — TDD tasks
+
+- Plan: [`plan.md`](./plan.md)
+- Issue: `b414a33f-aa82-4dfa-bf95-2cef1aca0e98`
+
+All tasks are sequential. DEV starts only after the pre-alpha human gate. Each app migration PR must stay at or below 300 added/modified production lines; tests, fixtures, and docs do not excuse an oversized migration diff. The verified-dead 319-line Meeting wrapper gets one separate deletion-only PR with zero replacement production code.
+
+## Task 1: Lock the shared product contract and import boundary
+
+**PR:** shared adapter foundation
+
+**OWNS:** `packages/ui-charting/package.json`, `packages/ui-charting/src/chart-contract.js`, `packages/ui-charting/src/chart-contract.test.js`, `packages/ui-charting/src/index.jsx`, `packages/ui-charting/src/index.d.ts`, `test/domain-inventory.test.js`, `bun.lock`
+
+**What to implement:** Exact-pin `@tanstack/charts` at the human-approved version (`0.9.0` only if pre-alpha is explicitly approved). Define plain product data/series/dimension/state/formatter contracts and engine-neutral selectors. Add a repository guard allowing TanStack imports only under `packages/ui-charting/src/engine/**`, rejecting floating chart versions and any new Recharts import/selector beyond an exact temporary debt allowlist for the inventoried consumers. Task 9 deletes the allowlist and turns the guard into zero tolerance.
+
+**TDD:** Write boundary and contract tests first; prove they fail on missing exports and on a synthetic unlisted engine occurrence; add the minimal contract/pin/guard plus exact debt allowlist; prove pass and inspect the root lock integrity.
+
+**Commit:** `test(charting): lock product chart boundary`
+
+**Expected:** engine types are unreachable from package declarations and the scan identifies every current app violation until later tasks remove it.
+
+## Task 2: Implement the shared TanStack engine and parity harness
+
+**PR:** shared adapter foundation
+
+**OWNS:** `packages/ui-charting/src/engine/tanstack-charts.jsx`, `packages/ui-charting/src/chart.jsx`, `packages/ui-charting/src/chart.test.jsx`, `packages/ui-charting/src/index.jsx`, `packages/ui-charting/src/index.d.ts`, `packages/ui-charting/package.json`
+
+**What to implement:** Map product contracts to memoized `0.9.0` definitions for time-series line/area, both bar orientations, donut, and radial gauge. Add `ChartFrame` ready/empty/loading/error behavior, required `accessibility: { label, description?, summary, tableCaption }`, adapter-derived exact-value table rows/columns from the plotted normalized data, stable summary/table IDs and `aria-describedby` linkage, engine-failure fallback, deterministic `initialWidth`, responsive height/aspect policy, stable product selectors, keyboard/pointer tooltip mapping, reduced motion, and product-owned SVG/raster export wrappers. Keep default SVG; no Canvas.
+
+**TDD:** First fail scene/SVG, SSR, DOM resize/cleanup, keyboard/tooltip, state, export, exact-value derivation/linkage, and engine-failure table tests from the plan matrix. Implement the smallest adapter, then refactor shared scale/tooltip/selector mapping while tests stay green.
+
+**Commit:** `feat(ui-charting): add isolated TanStack chart adapter`
+
+**Expected:** one package test command proves all supported families and cross-cutting contracts; authored production diff is reviewed and split if it becomes difficult to audit.
+
+## Task 3: Remove Platform's unused dependency
+
+**PR:** Platform cleanup (<=300 production lines)
+
+**OWNS:** `apps/platform-web/package.json`, `bun.lock`, `test/domain-inventory.test.js`
+
+**What to implement:** Remove the unused Recharts declaration/importer only. Do not add `ui-charting` until Platform has a real chart consumer.
+
+**TDD:** Add a failing manifest assertion, remove the declaration, regenerate the root lock, then run Platform lint/typecheck/tests/build plus the boundary test.
+
+**Commit:** `chore(platform-web): remove unused Recharts dependency`
+
+**Expected:** Platform has no chart engine dependency or behavior change.
+
+## Task 4: Migrate Meeting activity through ui-charting
+
+**PR:** Meeting migration (<=300 production lines)
+
+**OWNS:** `apps/meeting-web/package.json`, `apps/meeting-web/src/components/chart-area-interactive.jsx`, `apps/meeting-web/src/components/__tests__/chart-area-interactive.test.js`, `apps/meeting-web/vite.config.js`, `bun.lock`
+
+**What to implement:** Declare `@product-suite/ui-charting`, preserve `buildSeries` and the time-range controls, replace direct area/wrapper usage with `TimeSeriesChart`, preserve dates, two series, fills/strokes, 280px responsive behavior and accessible copy. Leave the now-unused local wrapper for Task 5.
+
+**TDD:** Extend the test from pure bucketing to rendered ready/empty states, stable selectors, accessible name, exact summary/caption/table headers and all 7/30/90-day values, table persistence on engine failure, responsive initial size, and pointer/keyboard tooltip values. Prove RED on current output, implement, then run Meeting lint/test/build and the boundary scan.
+
+**Commit:** `refactor(meeting-web): route activity chart through shared adapter`
+
+**Expected:** the active Meeting chart has no direct engine import or selector; the unused local wrapper remains the one explicitly tracked source debt for Task 5; chart behavior and range switching remain unchanged.
+
+## Task 5: Retire the dead Meeting Recharts wrapper
+
+**PR:** Meeting wrapper retirement (one deletion-only production file)
+
+**OWNS:** `apps/meeting-web/src/components/ui/chart.jsx`
+
+**What to implement:** Prove the 319-line wrapper has zero importers after Task 4, then delete exactly that file. Add no replacement production code and do not remove Recharts dependencies yet.
+
+**TDD:** Run the repository consumer scan and Meeting lint/test/build before deletion, delete the file, rerun the same commands and boundary debt inventory, and inspect the diff for one production-file deletion only.
+
+**Commit:** `chore(meeting-web): retire unused Recharts wrapper`
+
+**Expected:** Meeting has no Recharts source consumer; dependency retirement remains gated on the final all-app observation window.
+
+## Task 6: Migrate Roadmap analytics chart cards
+
